# NewScenario22 / Challenge130 — 5 routers (RIP), pc-3, server-4, docker-1, docker-2
#
# KNOWN RISK (see GOAD_Scenario_Build_Summary.md, Challenge101 session log):
# router-1 is the hub (r2r degree 4) and therefore needs 6 total adapters
# (NAT + management + 4 r2r links). On VMware Workstation this is the exact
# adapter count that previously triggered a PCI-bridge slot overflow, causing
# router-1's guest interface naming to desync from VMX slot order and 5 of
# its adapters to bind to the wrong vmnets. If router-1 comes up but is
# unreachable via plain `ssh` (while `vagrant ssh router-1` still works),
# see that session's "Major finding" section for the MAC-address-based
# GUI-bypass fix — do not rely on vagrant reload/halt/up to fix it, those
# will re-assert the wrong mapping every time.

